  "verbalization": "Nocapyrone G appears to be a compound that interacts with DNA polymerase eta through a series of target relationships, as evidenced by its association with SK-OV-3 cells, which are targeted by multiple compounds including (S)-3-cyclohexene-1-methanol, Linderoxide, and Alstoniaphylline A. These compounds all lead to DNA polymerase eta as their final target, suggesting a potential mechanism where Nocapyrone G may exert its effects through a shared pathway that ultimately affects DNA polymerase eta. The evidence indicates that Nocapyrone G could act as a modulator or inhibitor of DNA polymerase eta, possibly by targeting SK-OV-3 cells, which are a key cellular model for this interaction. The consistent presence of DNA polymerase eta as a target across different compounds supports the idea of a broader biological role for this enzyme in the context of the SK-OV-3 cell line. The integration of these findings suggests that Nocapyrone G may influence DNA polymerase eta through a mechanism that involves the SK-OV-3 cells, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
